AnimFrames←{
   ⍝ Planet data for the frames of an animation, at stated day numbers ⍺
   ⍝ ⍵ is TIME LAT LONG
   ⍝ Result is PX PY VIS RAH RAM DEC ALT AZ MX MY, each frames × 11 bodies
   ⍝ (rows padded when the comet is out of range), then the moon's phases
    t lat long←⍵
    frame←{
        sky←SkyAt ⍵ t lat long
        n←11-≢sky.Planets
        coord←(≢sky.Planets)2⍴0
        coord[⍸sky.PlanetsVisible;]←sky.PlanetCoord
        coord←coord⍪n 2⍴0
        bodies←sky.Planets⍪n 3⍴0
        aa←sky.PlanetsAA⍪n 2⍴¯90 0
        rah←⌊bodies[;1]
        px←⌊0.5+1160+1080×coord[;1]
        py←⌊0.5+1160-1080×coord[;2]
        ram←⌊0.5+60×bodies[;1]-rah
        dec←⌊0.5+bodies[;2]
        alt az←↓⌊0.5+⍉aa
        mx my←↓0.01×⌊0.5+100×⍉coord
        px py(sky.PlanetsVisible,n⍴0)rah ram dec alt az mx my sky.Phase
    }
    frames←frame¨,⍺
    ({↑⍵⊃¨frames}¨⍳10),⊂11⊃¨frames }
